# What gcloud uploads as build source. Separate from .dockerignore: that one only
# controls what lands in the image, and does NOT stop `gcloud run deploy --source .`
# from uploading a file to Cloud Storage. Client timesheet scans were reaching the
# staging bucket that way.
#
# Prefer ./deploy.sh, which builds from a temp dir containing only app files.

# Client timesheet scans and extracted CSVs — real employee data, never upload.
# Named explicitly rather than relying only on extension rules below:
# TIMEKEEPING/ and benchmark/ also hold .xlsx/.pdf/.json those don't catch.
# Glob, not a fixed list: each client drop arrives as a new reference<N>/ folder
# full of real scans, and a hand-maintained list silently misses the next one.
reference*/
reference/
reference2/
reference3/
TIMEKEEPING/
benchmark/
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.csv

# Secrets
.env

# Local-only tooling and docs
.git
.gitignore
docker-compose.yml
deploy.sh
*.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
